-- ═══ 353 RETIRE (duplicate of 742 under an invented title) ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 110) as a duplicate under an invented title. The University of Helsinki has no award called 'International Master Grant': its official 'Tuition fees and scholarship programme' page (fetched 2026-10-27; the URL stored on this row returns 404) states that the university's scholarship programme consists solely of tuition fee waivers of 50% or 100% for excellent tuition-fee-liable master's students from outside the EU/EEA and Switzerland - only a very limited number, most of them 50% - running two years conditional on at least 55 ECTS per year, applied for on the master's application form, and it states expressly that the University of Helsinki does not offer scholarships to cover living expenses. That real scheme is already catalogued accurately as record 742 ('University of Helsinki Scholarship Programme (Tuition Fee Waivers)', reliability 9), so this reliability-4 title - which additionally implies a living-cost 'grant' the university does not give - is retired rather than rewritten into a second copy of 742. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 590 withdrawn; source 2536 (previously the bare helsinki.fi domain) repointed to the official scholarship-programme page used for this determination.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 353;

-- ═══ 405 Aalto University Excellence Scholarship ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Aalto University Excellence Scholarship', provider = 'Aalto University', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'The scholarship is applied for inside the Aalto admission application itself (tick the scholarship option on the application form) - it must be requested during the programme''s application period, cannot be applied for afterwards, and the decision is given together with the admission decision (Studyinfo application rounds for autumn entry; see Aalto admissions for your programme''s dates).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Bachelor's", "Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["English-taught bachelor's and master's programmes at Aalto University (each programme decides its own scholarship allocation and may grant none; some international joint degree programmes run their own schemes instead)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Students liable for tuition fees in Finland (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens without an exempting residence permit)"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Aalto University Excellence Scholarship is Aalto's merit scholarship for outstanding tuition-fee-liable applicants: a tuition fee waiver covering the full tuition fee for the normative duration of the degree (three years for a bachelor's, two years for a master's), granted on a competitive basis to the highest-achieving applicants under each programme's evaluation criteria - in master's admissions the scholarships are allocated during the academic evaluation stage, and a programme may decide to grant none at all. Aalto is candid about scarcity: only a very limited number of scholarships are available, and they go to the top applicants. The waiver is valuable because Aalto's annual fees for study rights beginning on or after 1 August 2025 run from €12,000 to €15,000 at bachelor's level (Business/Technology/multidisciplinary €12,000; Art and Architecture €15,000) and from €15,000 to €20,000 at master's level (Business €15,000; Technology and multidisciplinary programmes €17,000; Art and Architecture €20,000). The scholarship covers no living costs - students must fund at least €800 per month of living expenses themselves - and it requires full-time study according to the approved personal study plan. It is applied for on the admission application form during the application period only (later scholarship applications are impossible), and the decision arrives with the admission decision. Two connected rules sit around it: new bachelor's students who accept their offer bindingly and pay within 21 days receive a 25% reduction on the first-year fee instead of any scholarship route, and Aalto bachelor's graduates who held the Excellence Scholarship, finished within three years with a weighted average grade of at least 3.5, and continue to an Aalto master's with direct study right receive a 100% waiver for the master's as well. Scholarship candidates are screened against the EU sanctions lists.$desc$, requirements = $req$Only applicants liable for tuition fees (citizens of countries outside the EU/EEA and Switzerland who hold no fee-exempting Finnish residence permit) may apply, and the scholarship option must be selected on the Aalto application form during the application period - an applicant who does not ask for it then cannot receive it later. Selection is purely on the programme's admission evaluation criteria: applicants are ranked per programme, the best fee-liable applicants may be awarded the full waiver, programmes may award none, and under the Finnish Universities Act the scholarship decision cannot be appealed. The scholarship runs for the normative study period and presumes full-time study following the approved personal study plan; it does not pay living expenses, study materials, the Student Union (AYY) fee or the student healthcare fee. No GPA figure or IELTS threshold is published at scholarship level (English requirements belong to each programme's admission rules), so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded. Candidates on EU sanctions lists are ineligible.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.aalto.fi/en/admission-services/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', source_url = 'https://www.aalto.fi/en/admission-services/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', application_url = 'https://www.aalto.fi/en/admission-services/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 110) from Aalto University's official 'Scholarships and Tuition Fees' page fetched the same day (Excellence Scholarships as full tuition fee waivers for the normative duration - 3 years bachelor's, 2 years master's - merit-based and competitive for the highest-achieving fee-liable applicants, very limited in number, programmes may grant none, allocated at the academic-evaluation stage with the decision given alongside admission and non-appealable; scholarship applied for on the admission form during the application period only; no living-cost coverage, at least €800/month to be self-funded; tuition fee table for study rights from 1 August 2025 - bachelor's €12,000/€15,000, master's €15,000/€17,000/€20,000 by field; 25% first-year early-acceptance reduction for new bachelor's students paying within 21 days; bachelor's-to-master's continuation waiver for Excellence holders graduating within target time with a weighted average of at least 3.5; EU sanctions screening; fee liability and residence-permit exemption rules as summarised in the text). The separate Pekka Mattila Excellence Scholarship (School of Business Marketing/International Management master's, €3,000 relocation grant) found on the same page is a different, narrower scheme and a future-additions candidate; international joint programmes have their own schemes. Award stored as NULL (EUR, 'year', 'variable'): a 100% waiver whose euro value follows the programme's €12,000-20,000 fee, per the percentage-waiver convention. Title normalised from the stored 'Aalto University Scholarship Programme' to the scheme's official name, and degree_levels corrected to Bachelor's + Master's (the stored row said Master's only). deadline_date NULL/'not_published': the scholarship deadline is each programme's admission application period, which this page does not date; status 'upcoming' for the coming autumn-entry round. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. university_scholarships row 100 synced; source 2476 repointed from the bare aalto.fi domain to the fetched official page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no terms read.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'EUR', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = '100% tuition fee waiver for the normative duration of the degree (3 years bachelor''s, 2 years master''s) for the highest-achieving fee-liable applicants; no living-cost support. (Separately: 25% first-year fee reduction for new bachelor''s students who accept and pay within 21 days.)', tuition_coverage = 'The waiver covers the full tuition fee (€12,000-15,000/year at bachelor''s level and €15,000-20,000/year at master''s level for study rights beginning on/after 1 August 2025, by field).', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure; English requirements are set by each degree programme''s admission criteria.', required_documents = $j$["Aalto admission application with the scholarship option selected during the application period (mandatory - the scholarship cannot be requested later)", "Proof of citizenship (passport/national ID) and, where applicable, copies of both sides of a Finnish residence permit card to determine fee liability", "Programme admission documents on which the academic ranking is based (scholarships follow the programme's evaluation criteria)"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern": "Annual, inside the admission application: tick the scholarship option during your programme's Studyinfo application period for autumn entry (master's applications typically late autumn-early winter, bachelor's in the January joint application - check Aalto admissions); the scholarship decision is issued together with the admission decision in spring"}]$json$ WHERE id = 405;

-- ═══ 504 University of Turku Merit Scholarship and Early Bird Discount ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'University of Turku Merit Scholarship and Early Bird Discount', provider = 'University of Turku', coverage_type = 'Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No first-year scholarship exists: new master''s students instead get a €2,000 Early Bird discount by accepting the study offer and paying the first-year fee within 28 days of the admission decisions (for 2026 admission, by 24 April 2026). The Merit Scholarship has its own application round each spring - Admission Services invite all eligible continuing students to apply for the following year''s 50% waiver.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Bachelor's", "Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Tuition-fee-liable bachelor's and master's degree programmes at the University of Turku (programme-specific fees mostly €10,000-12,000/year; the merit rules are university-wide)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Students liable for tuition fees in Finland (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens without an exempting residence permit)"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$Turku's model is the classic Finnish progress-based one, and it must be read carefully: it is not possible to get a scholarship to cover the tuition fee for the first year. What a new master's student can get instead is an Early Bird discount of €2,000 for accepting the study offer and paying the first-year tuition fee within 28 days after the admission decisions are published (for the 2026 intake the payment deadline for the discount was 24 April 2026; the discount is not available for bachelor's applicants). The actual scholarship - the University of Turku Merit Scholarship - starts from the second year and is awarded purely on studies completed at Turku: it covers 50% of the following year's tuition fee, and every tuition-fee-liable student who fulfils the published requirements receives it (it is rule-based, not a ranked competition). For master's students the scholarship covers 50% of the second-year fee after completing 55 credits in the first study year. For bachelor's students it covers 50% of the second-year fee after 55 credits in the first year, and 50% of the third-year fee after 110 credits across the first two years. All applicants must also hold a study-average grade of at least 3.0 on the Finnish 1-5 scale and have completed at least 4 credits of Finnish language studies before their first scholarship application (these may count within the 55 credits; other proven Finnish proficiency is assessed case by case). There is a separate scholarship application each spring, with Admission Services inviting eligible students to apply. Against programme fees of mostly €10,000-12,000 a year, the 50% waiver is worth roughly €5,000-6,000 in the second (and, for bachelor's, third) year - but the full first year must always be financed by the student (minus the master's Early Bird €2,000).$desc$, requirements = $req$Eligible students are tuition-fee-liable bachelor's and master's students who have paid for their studies in their first year(s) at the University of Turku and then meet three requirements before the spring scholarship application: the credit requirement (55 credits in the first study year for the second-year waiver; bachelor's students additionally 110 credits across years one and two for the third-year waiver), the grade requirement (an average of at least 3.0 on the Finnish 1-5 grading scale), and the Finnish-language requirement (at least 4 completed credits of Finnish before the first application, which may sit inside the 55 credits, or other accepted proof of Finnish proficiency). All students fulfilling the requirements are awarded the scholarship for the following academic year - it is academic-merit rule-based, not quota-limited. The 3.0 average is on Finland's 1-5 scale and is a continuation criterion for current students, so it is described textually and min_gpa is not recorded; no IELTS figure applies. Note the hard sequencing: the first-year fee is never waived by this scheme, the €2,000 Early Bird discount is master's-only and demands payment within 28 days of the admission decisions, and the first-year fee must be paid before registration at the university.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.utu.fi/en/study-at-utu/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', source_url = 'https://www.utu.fi/en/study-at-utu/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', application_url = 'https://www.utu.fi/en/study-at-utu/scholarships-and-tuition-fees', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 110) from the University of Turku's official 'Tuition fees and scholarships' page fetched the same day (page states it is for students admitted in 2026: no scholarship for the first-year fee; €2,000 Early Bird discount for master's applicants who accept the offer and pay within 28 days of the admission decisions - final date 24 April 2026 for that intake - and not for bachelor's applicants; the University of Turku Merit Scholarship covering 50% of the next year's tuition fee for every fee-liable student who fulfils the requirements - 55 credits in year one for the master's year-two and bachelor's year-two waivers, 110 credits across years one and two for the bachelor's year-three waiver; average grade at least 3.0 on the 1-5 scale; at least 4 credits of Finnish before the first application; separate spring application round with invitations from Admission Services; programme-specific fees listed at €10,000-12,000 with one €1,500 exception). The Fulbright-University of Turku Graduate Award mentioned on the page is US-citizen-only and outside this record's identity. Award stored as NULL (EUR, 'year', 'variable'): a 50% waiver whose euro value depends on the programme fee, plus the fixed €2,000 first-year discount described in funding_type. Title normalised to the official scheme names. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (the only dated round on the fetched page, 24 April 2026, has passed; both the Early Bird window and the spring merit-scholarship round recur annually with each admission cycle, recorded in rounds); status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (the 3.0/5 continuation average is textual). university_scholarships row 455 synced; source 997 repointed from the bare utu.fi/en root to the fetched official page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no terms read.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'EUR', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Merit Scholarship: 50% tuition fee waiver from the second year onward for every fee-liable student meeting the credit (55 cr/year; 110 cr across years 1-2 for a bachelor''s third year), grade (average >= 3.0/5) and Finnish-language (>= 4 cr) requirements. First year: €2,000 Early Bird discount for master''s students who accept and pay within 28 days - no first-year scholarship.', tuition_coverage = '50% of the tuition fee from the second study year onward (fees mostly €10,000-12,000/year, so typically €5,000-6,000 waived per eligible year); the first-year fee is payable in full (minus the €2,000 master''s Early Bird discount).', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure; language requirements follow each programme''s admission rules. Note the inverse condition: 4 credits of Finnish are required to unlock the merit scholarship.', required_documents = $j$["For the Early Bird discount: accept the study offer and pay the first-year tuition fee within 28 days after the admission decisions", "For the Merit Scholarship: application in the spring round (Admission Services invite eligible students) evidencing 55 completed credits (or 110 across two years for the bachelor's third year)", "Study transcript showing an average grade of at least 3.0 on the 1-5 scale and at least 4 completed credits of Finnish"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"intake": "2026 admission (page edition)", "early_bird_pay_by": "2026-04-24", "status": "closed"}, {"pattern": "Annual: master's Early Bird discount if the offer is accepted and the first-year fee paid within 28 days of the admission decisions; a separate spring application round awards the 50% Merit Scholarship for the following year on completed Turku studies"}]$json$ WHERE id = 504;

-- ═══ 505 University of Oulu waivers ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'University of Oulu Partial Tuition Fee Waiver Scholarships and Early Bird Discounts', provider = 'University of Oulu', coverage_type = 'Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'The first year is never waived by scholarship; instead, selected programmes give an Early Bird discount (5-30%, programme-specific) when the tuition fee is paid within three weeks of the admission results. The partial tuition fee waiver scholarships apply automatically from the second year onwards on study progress - at least 60 ECTS completed in the preceding academic year under the approved study plan (including the programme''s Finnish language studies).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Bachelor's", "Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["English-taught bachelor's and master's programmes at the University of Oulu - percentages are programme-specific (one master's programme, Epidemiology and Biomedical Data Science, offers neither Early Bird discount nor a waiver in the current table)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Students liable for tuition fees in Finland (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens without an exempting residence permit)"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The University of Oulu publishes the most itemised of the Finnish progress-based waiver tables, and its shape is the same at both levels: pay the first year yourself, then earn a partial waiver by progressing on schedule. For the first year, selected programmes offer an Early Bird discount when the tuition fee is paid within three weeks of the admission results - at master's level most programmes discount 30% (e.g. a €10,000 fee falls to €7,000 and a €12,000 fee to €8,400), with smaller 5-15% discounts in a few programmes; the four English-taught bachelor's programmes (all €10,000 a year) discount 30%. From the second year onwards, the partial Tuition Fee Waiver Scholarships are awarded on successful study progress: the student must complete at least 60 ECTS credits during the preceding academic year in accordance with the approved study plan, including the Finnish language studies whose scope differs by programme. The waiver percentage is fixed per programme for the intake and ranges from 10% to 40% - for example 40% in Architecture (fee €14,000, so €8,400 payable), Chemistry of Sustainable Processes and Materials and Environmental Engineering; 30% across most technology programmes; 20% in the Oulu Business School master's programmes and the bachelor's International Business Management (rising to 30% in its master's phase); 15% in Biochemistry; and 10% in Education for Global Futures and Leadership; Epidemiology and Biomedical Data Science offers neither discount nor waiver. Master's tuition fees in the current table run from €8,500 to €14,000 a year. The page edition fetched applies to students admitted in the autumn 2026 and spring 2027 rounds for studies beginning in 2027-2028, so its percentages are live for the coming intake; continuing-student administration sits on a separate Oulu page.$desc$, requirements = $req$Both instruments belong to tuition-fee-liable students (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens in English-taught programmes without a fee-exempting residence permit). The Early Bird discount requires only speed: pay the first-year fee within three weeks of the published admission results (confirming the study place first is strongly recommended but not required before payment), in a programme that offers the discount. The year-two-onwards waiver requires progress exactly on the degree's rails: at least 60 ECTS credits in the preceding academic year under the approved personal study plan, including the Finnish language studies prescribed for the programme - falling behind that pace means paying the full fee again. No grade-average condition is published for the waiver (the criterion is completed credits under the plan), and no IELTS figure applies at scholarship level, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded. Percentages are intake- and programme-specific and may change between admission rounds; they do not cover living expenses, the fee itself excludes accommodation, meals and transport, and the first year must always be financed by the student (minus any Early Bird discount).$req$, website_url = 'https://www.oulu.fi/en/apply/how-apply/university-oulu-tuition-fees-and-scholarships-for-international-applicants', source_url = 'https://www.oulu.fi/en/apply/how-apply/university-oulu-tuition-fees-and-scholarships-for-international-applicants', application_url = 'https://www.oulu.fi/en/apply/how-apply', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 110) from the University of Oulu's official 'tuition fees and scholarships for international applicants' page fetched the same day (page states it applies to students admitted in the autumn 2026 or spring 2027 rounds for studies beginning 2027-2028; Early Bird discount for selected programmes when the fee is paid within three weeks of the admission results - 30% for the four English-taught bachelor's programmes and for most master's programmes, 5-15% in a few, unavailable in Epidemiology and Biomedical Data Science; partial Tuition Fee Waiver Scholarships from the second year onwards on at least 60 ECTS completed in the preceding academic year under the approved study plan including programme-specific Finnish language studies, with programme-fixed percentages of 10-40% across master's programmes (40% Architecture/Chemistry of Sustainable Processes/Environmental Engineering; 30% most technology; 20% business school; 15% Biochemistry; 10% Education for Global Futures and Leadership; none for Epidemiology and Biomedical Data Science) and 20-30% at bachelor's level (International Business Management 20% bachelor's rising to 30% in the master's phase); annual fees €8,500-14,000 master's and €10,000 bachelor's; fee-liability exemptions as listed on the page). Award stored as NULL (EUR, 'year', 'variable'): percentage waivers and discounts whose euro values depend on the programme fee and the intake table. Title normalised to the official scheme names. deadline_date NULL/'not_published': the only deadlines are the three-week Early Bird payment window after each round's results and the year-by-year credit condition, both recorded in rounds; status 'upcoming' because the fetched page edition governs the autumn 2026/spring 2027 admission rounds now opening. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (the waiver condition is 60 ECTS of progress, not a grade average). university_scholarships row 456 synced; source 916 repointed from the bare oulu.fi/en root to the fetched official page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no terms read.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'EUR', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Partial tuition fee waiver scholarships from year 2 onward at programme-fixed rates of 10-40% (master''s; 20-30% bachelor''s), conditional on completing at least 60 ECTS per year under the approved study plan incl. Finnish studies; first year has only programme-specific Early Bird discounts (5-30%) for payment within three weeks of results.', tuition_coverage = '10-40% of the annual tuition fee waived from the second year onwards depending on the programme (fees €8,500-14,000/year master''s, €10,000/year for the English bachelor''s programmes) - e.g. 30% takes a €10,000 fee to €7,000; the first year is payable in full minus any Early Bird discount.', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure; English requirements follow each programme''s admission rules. Note the progress condition includes the programme''s Finnish language studies.', required_documents = $j$["For the Early Bird discount: pay the first-year tuition fee within three weeks of the admission results (programe must offer the discount)", "For the waiver from year 2: study record showing at least 60 ECTS completed in the preceding academic year under the approved study plan, including the required Finnish language studies"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"edition": "Autumn 2026 / spring 2027 admission rounds (studies beginning 2027-2028)", "status": "upcoming"}, {"pattern": "Annual: Early Bird discount (5-30% by programme) for fees paid within three weeks of the admission results; partial waivers (10-40% by programme) then apply from the second year onwards while the student completes at least 60 ECTS a year under the study plan"}]$json$ WHERE id = 505;

